From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petar Tijanic <Petar_Tijanic@comcast.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] evdev: fix the d-pad hat index

The hat index for the mapping lookup was key_map[hat_number] * 2 + axis, but
key_map is the button map - indexing it by a hat ordinal returns a button value
(a home button can land at key_map[0]) and the d-pad stops working on some
controllers. The mapping stores hat bindings at hat_number * 2 + axis, which is
just (code - ABS_HAT0X). Forward-ports the 0.2 nintendo dpad fix; the analog
trigger detection half is dropped since 1.0 exposes triggers as axes.
---
diff --git a/src/manette-evdev-backend.c b/src/manette-evdev-backend.c
index e8bb474..b1631df 100644
--- a/src/manette-evdev-backend.c
+++ b/src/manette-evdev-backend.c
@@ -344,9 +344,10 @@ on_evdev_event (ManetteEvdevBackend *self,
     case ABS_HAT2Y:
     case ABS_HAT3X:
     case ABS_HAT3Y:
-      guint index =
-        self->key_map[(evdev_event->code - ABS_HAT0X) / 2] * 2 +
-        (evdev_event->code - ABS_HAT0X) % 2;
+      /* (code - ABS_HAT0X) is hat_number*2 + axis, the index the mapping wants.
+       * Don't run the hat number through key_map (the button map) - it returns a
+       * button value and breaks the dpad. */
+      guint index = evdev_event->code - ABS_HAT0X;
 
       manette_backend_emit_unmapped_hat_event (MANETTE_BACKEND (self), time,
                                                index, evdev_event->value);
--
